---

You need **NeoForge 1.21.1**, [Iron’s Spells ’n Spellbooks](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/irons-spells-n-spellbooks), and Iron’s Lib. Drop Spell Actionbar in `mods` with those two.

Open a world and press the Actionbar key. Default is the backtick, the one under Escape. That opens the equip screen. Put an Iron’s **scroll** in a slot, close the menu, and the bar appears above your hotbar.

Cast with Iron’s **quick-cast** keys, not a second set of binds. The little label on each slot is whatever Minecraft currently has bound. If a slot shows `Q`, that’s your Q.

Scrolls on the bar are not eaten. You can sit on Fireball all afternoon.

The bar stays hidden until you actually equip something. That’s on purpose. Empty worlds don’t get a dead HUD.

If you also install [Spell Codex](/mods/spell-codex), stop thinking in loose scrolls. Codex decides which spells you own. You still use this same bar to cast, and Codex wants Actionbar **1.1.4 or newer**.
